<title>UK: EU seen awarding up to 30,000 T sugar at tender.</title>
<headline>EU seen awarding up to 30,000 T sugar at tender.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union (EU) is expected to award up to 30,000 tonnes of current series white sugar at its weekly tender later on Wednesday, traders said.</p>
<p>Last week the EU awarded 38,550 tonnes in its tender.</p>
<p>This week's maximum restitution level was estimated at 44.166 Ecus (European currency units) per 100 kilos of sugar after the 43.862 Ecus awarded last week.</p>
<p>Licences are currently valid until the end of August.</p>
<p>Cumulatively, the tonnage awards for 1996/97 are still lagging behind the equivalent stage in 1995/96</p>
<p>As of March 12, this year's total stood at 1,636,450 tonnes, compared with 1,647,148 tonnes on March 13, 1996.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
